{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Crooked.</b> Po'el form, like מדובר, and they are two roots but the meaning is one: whole and that which is not whole. The word לתקון is a verbal noun in construct state, and the meaning follows the first interpretation of the two verses preceding this one: after he saw that all is הבל, the הבל cannot turn back as standing, for the crooked cannot be made straight, for its nature is crooked, and that which has a deficiency has no power to be counted among the whole. And this is the interpretation of חסרון: one who has a deficiency — or it is an adjective, like ראשון and ארחון — or it refers back to מעוות, and מעוות alone is in its nature crooked, and חסרון is deficient in its deficiency. And according to the second interpretation: born in a deficient arrangement, it has no power to complete itself. And so one who occupies himself investigating the essence of phenomena from the work of the heavens engages in תוהו. And this holds true for the majority of people and the majority of their deeds."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "I read בעל מחסרון and the repetition of מעוות / חסרון as Ibn Ezra's characteristic compressed listing of multiple grammatical analyses of the phrase; the run-on structure is preserved as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:06.242685890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}